       "elements": [
        {
         "id": "4499d86",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "What does a first therapy session involve?",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "3386ce1",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>A first session is usually a conversation about what has brought you, how long it has been going on, and what you would like to be different. The therapist may ask what you have already tried and whether anything is urgent. You can ask how they work, how often they would expect to see you, and what happens if you want to stop.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "0cd79e0",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>It can feel awkward. Most people find the first ten minutes the hardest. You do not have to tell the whole story, and you do not have to be articulate about it. “I do not know where to start” is a normal first sentence.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "48c07dd",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>Nothing needs to be decided in the room. Most therapists expect you to go away and think about whether it felt right, and will say so.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "7753eda",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "How much does therapy cost?",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "83d7c58",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>Private therapists set their own fees, and the fee is printed on the profile when the therapist has entered it. Where it is not, ask in your first message. You are allowed to ask about cost before anything else, and a therapist will not think less of you for it. Some offer a smaller number of reduced-fee places; the profile says so where that is the case.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "dfe0d5a",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>Gototherapy does not type a typical fee or a range anywhere on the site. Where a range appears in future, it is computed from what members have entered, on the day you look.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "0cf3186",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>If you cannot pay, you should not leave with nothing. In England you can refer yourself to NHS Talking Therapies without seeing a GP, and your GP can also refer you. Waiting times vary by area. Elsewhere in the UK, your GP is the usual route.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "56b3e6f",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "heading",
         "settings": {
          "title": "How do I know if it is the right fit?",
          "header_size": "h2",
          "_css_classes": "gt-h2"
         },
         "elements": []
        },
        {
         "id": "0bade65",
         "elType": "widget",
         "widgetType": "text-editor",
         "settings": {
          "editor": "<p>After two or three sessions you should be able to answer three questions. Do you feel listened to. Do you feel able to say when something does not land. Does the therapist explain what they are doing when you ask. If the answer to any of these is no, say so in the session. If it does not change, it is reasonable to try somebody else. Changing therapist is not a failure and does not need a justification.</p>",
          "_css_classes": ""
         },
         "elements": []
        }
       ],
       "isInner": true
